    "q-218423": {
      "dom_id": "step-q218423",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "Evaluate the following expression. Use $i$ to denote the imaginary unit.\n\n$(-5+12\\,\\text{i})+(6-9\\,\\text{i})=$\n{{field-1}}",
      "worked_solution": "Given the complex number $a+b\\,\\text{i},$ $a$ represents its real part while $b$ represents its imaginary part.\n\nTo add or subtract complex numbers, we add or subtract their real parts, and we add or subtract their imaginary parts.\n\nFor the given problem, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(-5+12\\,\\text{i})+(6-9\\,\\text{i}) & =(-5+6)+(12+(-9))\\,\\text{i} \\\\  & =(-5+6)+(12-9)\\,\\text{i} \\\\  & =1+3\\,\\text{i}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
