    "q-597": {
      "dom_id": "step-q597",
      "name": "Question 4",
      "problem": "$(9+8\\,\\text{i})-(6+4\\,\\text{i})=$",
      "worked_solution": "Given the complex number $a+b\\,\\text{i},$ $a$ represents its real part while $b$ represents its imaginary part.\n\nTo add or subtract complex numbers, we add or subtract their real parts, and we add or subtract their imaginary parts.\n\nFor the given problem, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(9+8\\,\\text{i})-(6+4\\,\\text{i}) & =(9-6)+(8-4)\\,\\text{i} \\\\  & =3+4\\,\\text{i}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
