    "q-250273": {
      "dom_id": "step-q250273",
      "name": "Question 5",
      "problem": "Expressed as a complex number,\n\n$(11-\\sqrt{-80})-(6+\\sqrt{-125})=$\n{{field-1}}$-\\,$\n{{field-2}}$\\text{i}.$",
      "worked_solution": "Given the complex number $a+b\\,\\text{i},$ $a$ represents its real part while $b$ represents its imaginary part.\n\nTo add or subtract complex numbers, we add or subtract their real parts, and we add or subtract their imaginary parts.\n\nFor the given problem, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(11-\\sqrt{-80})-(6+\\sqrt{-125}) & =(11-\\sqrt{16\\cdot 5}\\,\\text{i})-(6+\\sqrt{25\\cdot 5}\\,\\text{i}) \\\\  & =(11-4\\sqrt{5}\\,\\text{i})-(6+5\\sqrt{5}\\,\\text{i}) \\\\  & =(11-6)+(-4\\sqrt{5}-5\\sqrt{5})\\,\\text{i} \\\\  & =5-9\\sqrt{5}\\,\\text{i}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
