    "q-250309": {
      "dom_id": "step-q250309",
      "name": "Question 8",
      "problem": "Evaluate the following expression. Use $i$ to denote the imaginary unit.\n\n$-5\\,\\text{i}-8\\,\\text{i}=$\n{{field-1}}",
      "worked_solution": "To add or subtract complex numbers, we add or subtract their real parts, and we add or subtract their imaginary parts.\n\nIn this case, $-5\\,\\text{i}$ and $8\\,\\text{i}$ are purely imaginary numbers. Therefore, we only need to add their imaginary parts, as follows:\n\n$$\n-5\\,\\text{i}-8\\,\\text{i}=(-5-8)\\,\\text{i}=-13\\,\\text{i}\n$$",
